{"oai_response": {"id": "chatcmpl-a3819280dc4c50e1", "created": 1787271560, "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b", "object": "chat.completion", "system_fingerprint": "vllm-0.26.0-tp8-6b7faac2", "choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "message": {"content": "```python\nimport sys\nfrom collections import deque\n\ndef build_automaton(pattern):\n    \"\"\"Builds the KMP automaton (transition table) for a given pattern.\"\"\"\n    m = len(pattern)\n    # Compute prefix function (pi array)\n    pi = [0] * m\n    for i in range(1, m):\n        j = pi[i - 1]\n        while j > 0 and pattern[i] != pattern[j]:\n            j = pi[j - 1]\n        if pattern[i] == pattern[j]:\n            j += 1\n        pi[i] = j\n\n    # Build transition table: trans[state][char] -> next_state\n    # states are 0..m. state m is the terminal \"virus found\" state.\n    trans = [[0] * 26 for _ in range(m + 1)]\n    for state in range(m + 1):\n        for c_idx in range(26):\n            char = chr(ord('A') + c_idx)\n            if state < m and char == pattern[state]:\n                trans[state][c_idx] = state + 1\n            else:\n                if state == 0:\n                    trans[state][c_idx] = 0\n                else:\n                    # Follow failure link (pi[state-1])\n                    trans[state][c_idx] = trans[pi[state - 1]][c_idx]\n    return trans\n\ndef solve():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().splitlines()\n    if len(data) < 3:\n        return\n    s1 = data[0].strip()\n    s2 = data[1].strip()\n    virus = data[2].strip()\n\n    n1 = len(s1)\n    n2 = len(s2)\n    m = len(virus)\n\n    trans = build_automaton(virus)\n\n    # dp[i][j][k] = max length of common subsequence of s1[i:] and s2[j:] with current virus state k\n    # Initialize with -inf (unreachable)\n    NEG_INF = -10**9\n    dp = [[[NEG_INF] * m for _ in range(n2 + 1)] for _ in range(n1 + 1)]\n\n    # Base case: end of strings, length 0 for all valid states\n    for k in range(m):\n        dp[n1][n2][k] = 0\n    \n    # Fill DP table bottom-up\n    for i in range(n1, -1, -1):\n        for j in range(n2, -1, -1):\n            if i == n1 and j == n2:\n                continue\n            for k in range(m):\n                best = NEG_INF\n                \n                # Option 1: Skip s1[i]\n                if i < n1:\n                    best = max(best, dp[i+1][j][k])\n                \n                # Option 2: Skip s2[j]\n                if j < n2:\n                    best = max(best, dp[i][j+1][k])\n                \n                # Option 3: Take s1[i] == s2[j]\n                if i < n1 and j < n2 and s1[i] == s2[j]:\n                    c_idx = ord(s1[i]) - ord('A')\n                    next_k = trans[k][c_idx]\n                    # Only proceed if virus is not fully matched (next_k < m)\n                    if next_k < m:\n                        val = 1 + dp[i+1][j+1][next_k]\n                        best = max(best, val)\n                \n                dp[i][j][k] = best\n\n    max_len = dp[0][0][0]\n    \n    if max_len <= 0:\n        print(0)\n        return\n\n    # Reconstruct the sequence\n    res = []\n    i, j, k = 0, 0, 0\n    while i < n1 and j < n2:\n        current_val = dp[i][j][k]\n        \n        # Check if we took the character\n        took_char = False\n        if s1[i] == s2[j]:\n            c_idx = ord(s1[i]) - ord('A')\n            next_k = trans[k][c_idx]\n            if next_k < m:\n                if 1 + dp[i+1][j+1][next_k] == current_val:\n                    res.append(s1[i])\n                    i += 1\n                    j += 1\n                    k = next_k\n                    took_char = True\n        \n        if took_char:\n            continue\n            \n        # Otherwise, we skipped one\n        # Check skip s1\n        if i < n1 and dp[i+1][j][k] == current_val:\n            i += 1\n        # Check skip s2\n        elif j < n2 and dp[i][j+1][k] == current_val:\n            j += 1\n        else:\n            # Should not happen if logic is correct, but break to avoid infinite loop\n            break\n            \n    print(\"\".join(res))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```", "role": "assistant", "provider_specific_fields": {"refusal": null, "reasoning": null}}, "provider_specific_fields": {"stop_reason": null, "token_ids": null, "routed_experts": null}}], "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1104, "prompt_tokens": 324, "total_tokens": 1428}}, "source_data": {"prob_desc_input_from": "standard input", "lang": "Python", "src_uid": "391c2abbe862139733fcb997ba1629b8", "difficulty": 2000, "prob_desc_sample_inputs": "[\"AJKEQSLOBSROFGZ\\nOVGURWZLWVLUXTH\\nOZ\", \"AA\\nA\\nA\"]", "prob_desc_time_limit": "3 seconds", "tags": ["dp", "strings"], "prob_desc_output_spec": "Output the longest common subsequence of s1 and s2 without virus as a substring. If there are multiple answers, any of them will be accepted.  If there is no valid common subsequence, output 0.", "prob_desc_input_spec": "The input contains three strings in three separate lines: s1, s2 and virus (1\u2009\u2264\u2009|s1|,\u2009|s2|,\u2009|virus|\u2009\u2264\u2009100). Each string consists only of uppercase English letters.", "lang_cluster": "Python", "source_code": "", "prob_desc_notes": null, "prob_desc_memory_limit": "512 megabytes", "file_name": "f4ed0b00bb6e7ee08ac776c854815632126f0d5842ed19563ab75f1660d87635", "code_uid": "", "prob_desc_description": "In mathematics, a subsequence is a sequence that can be derived from another sequence by deleting some elements without changing the order of the remaining elements. For example, the sequence BDF is a subsequence of ABCDEF. A substring of a string is a continuous subsequence of the string. For example, BCD is a substring of ABCDEF.You are given two strings s1, s2 and another string called virus. Your task is to find the longest common subsequence of s1 and s2, such that it doesn't contain virus as a substring.", "prob_desc_out